Key Changes Summary:

1. Proper map cleanup - Complete removal of previous map instance before creating a new one
2. Retry logic - Creates the map with up to 3 retry attempts if tile loading fails
3. Sequenced initialization - Map is created after data loads with proper delay
4. Container validation - Checks that map container exists before initialization
5. Error handling - Graceful fallback messages if libraries aren't loaded

These changes ensure the map loads reliably even with the new async features added to your application.
